  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the best at 0.6776 acc, and we've established scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 and weighted > concat. However, the image modality alone is very weak (0.3275 with resnet50), so it's unclear whether the image contribution is bottlenecked by encoder capacity. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l improve the multimodal model while holding the best-known RNA encoder (scvi_n200), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (weighted) fixed? This is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005. Why this is the best next experiment: it directly extends the current best configuration along the highest-uncertainty axis (image representation quality), and the result will tell us whether further investment in image-side design is worthwhile or whether the RNA signal dominates regardless of image encoder strength."
}

